KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ no access: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dereference failure.*: FAILURE$
--
N5008 [expr.context]/2, [conv.lval]/1: `(void)r' is a discarded-value
expression; for a non-volatile object no lvalue-to-rvalue conversion is
applied, so the object r refers to is not accessed.  The front end
dereferences r and reports "dereference failure: deallocated dynamic
object in *r" after `delete p'.  Also fails on bin53.  g++ 13 (with
-fsanitize=address) and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
